# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored — never commit a real token.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WEBFLOW_API_TOKEN belongs in `.dev.vars`, NOT here and NOT in `.env`.
#
# Two different consumers want it, and only one of them reads this file:
#
#   The app, at render time — src/lib/webflow/cms.ts reads the Blogs collection.
#   It needs `cms:read`, and it reads from the Worker environment, which locally
#   means `.dev.vars` and in Webflow Cloud means a Secret env var on the
#   environment. That is the one that matters.
#
#   The CLI, for `npm run devlink:export`. It does not need a token at all when
#   an OAuth session exists — `npx webflow auth login` — and that session
#   carries broader scopes than a hand-made token usually does.
#
# Setting it in `.env` shadows the OAuth session. That is how a deploy came to
# fail for a missing `sites:write` the session actually had. Leave it empty here
# unless you know you want the CLI using a specific token.
#
# Mint one at: Site settings → Apps & integrations → API access → Generate
# token. CMS read-only is enough. Scopes cannot be added to a token later — you
# mint a new one — and a site can hold five.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WEBFLOW_API_TOKEN=

# Optional. The site is already pinned as `siteId` in webflow.json
# (6a73c4d12df78ea4c276a06b — the "Stone" site). Setting this overrides it.
# WEBFLOW_SITE_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Agentbox --
# Reapit Sales (Agentbox) API credentials. Used only by
# `npm run agentbox:probe`, which fetches one listing so the field mapping in
# src/lib/ingestion/agentbox-mapping.ts can be checked against reality.
#
# The probe reads these from the environment or from `.dev.vars`. Both are
# gitignored. In Webflow Cloud they are environment variables of type Secret,
# set per environment.
#
# AGENTBOX_CLIENT_ID is base64 of the Agentbox admin URL, and it is what
# selects the instance. The client refuses one that does not decode to a
# sandbox unless asked to allow production explicitly.
AGENTBOX_CLIENT_ID=
AGENTBOX_API_KEY=

# Put the real values in `.dev.vars`, not here — this file is committed.
#
# Sandbox is the default, and the scripts refuse a client ID that does not
# decode to one. When the production credentials arrive, opt in per-run with
# `--allow-production`, or set this in a shell that only holds live keys.
# AGENTBOX_ALLOW_PRODUCTION=true
